//! 🧬️ Din4108 artifact — document mutation dispatch. Semantic vocabulary derived from
//! `📸️snapshot/🦀️.rs`'s `Din4108Snapshot` shape (seventeen document-root scalars +
//! `layers`, an index-keyed, id-less ordered construction build-up) per
//! `.🧬semio/🦑️repo/🎫️tickets/🎆️26/🌙️08/☀️12/SEMANTIC-MUTATIONS-OVERHAUL/📓️taxonomy.md`/
//! `📓️derivation-rules.md`. `impl protocol::Mutation`/`SemanticMutation` below are generated by
//! `#[derive(dsl::Mutations)]` — never hand-written.
//!
//! Every scalar field gets its own `change-<field>` leaf (rule 1's default — none of these fields
//! are documented as an inseparable, jointly-validated facet, so no `update-<facet>` grouping is
//! invented). `layers: Vec<LayerDocument>` has no stable id (rule 3): `insert-layer`/`remove-layer`
//! address by index (inserted = FINAL-state, removed = BASE-state), `reorder-layers` moves one
//! layer within the build-up, and `change-layer-thickness`/`change-layer-lambda` edit one field of
//! one layer by BASE-state index.
//!
//! Every triad leaf is mounted directly as a `mutations`-sibling module in `🦀️.rs` (this lane's
//! agent owns `🦀️.rs`, so no self-wiring `#[path = "."]` blocks are needed here — the orphaned
//! `🟤️set-snapshot` stub is deleted along with its dangling glue mount). That covers the PRODUCTION
//! mounts only: the handcrafted mutation-fixture tests in `🧪️FixtureTests` at the foot of this file
//! ARE self-wired with `#[path = "."]`, because `🦀️.rs` is shared with the agents migrating the
//! other thirteen norm artifacts and must not absorb this artifact's test mounts.

